; Local FPGA execution spec for Canon-bridged primitives.
;
; This file is fpga-lisp's own authority over HOW a Canon semantic
; identity (my-lisp's lib/surface/semantic-registry.wsm) is executed
; on this machine -- it does not define WHAT the identity means (that
; stays my-lisp's authority) and it does not change any existing
; opcode, TAG_PRIMITIVE numbering, or PRIM_* value in
; fpga/asm/constants.inc. It is the missing link tools/gen_primitive_table.py
; needs to build a generated Canon-id -> local-execution table instead
; of the identity being re-typed by hand in eval_core.inc, old test
; .asm files, and any future consumer.
;
; Format: (canon-id expected-en-spelling local-primitive-id opcode)
;   canon-id             -- semantic-registry.wsm's numeric id (string, 4 digits)
;   expected-en-spelling -- sanity cross-check only: if the registry's
;                           "en" surface for this id is present, it must
;                           equal this word, or generation fails closed.
;                           If the registry's en surface is "missing"
;                           for this id (e.g. 0104/add has no en entry
;                           yet), the check is skipped, not failed.
;   local-primitive-id   -- must equal the matching PRIM_* value in
;                           fpga/asm/constants.inc (cross-checked by the
;                           generator, not just asserted here).
;   opcode                -- the hardware mechanism name, informational
;                           for now (fpga-lisp does not yet have every
;                           listed name as a literal top-level opcode --
;                           car/cdr/cons/atom/eq are dispatched through
;                           try_apply's primitive path in eval_core.inc,
;                           add likewise via PRIM_ADD -- "OP_*" here
;                           names the mechanism, not a promise that a
;                           same-named top-level ISA opcode exists).
;
; Adding an entry here does NOT create hardware. It documents which
; already-existing local primitive a Canon identity maps to. Removing
; or renumbering an entry needs the same care as touching constants.inc
; itself -- see that file's own header.

(fpga-primitive-execution-spec
  (0005 car  0 OP_CAR)
  (0006 cdr  1 OP_CDR)
  (0004 cons 2 OP_CONS)
  (0002 atom 3 OP_ATOM)
  (0003 eq   4 OP_EQ)
  (0104 add  5 OP_ADD)
)
